{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3872","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3872","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3872\",\"parent_revision\":\"579aac2e9162465e62af4084d0b662134915b6d4b6a92024a60e149c12e3410d\",\"root_revision\":\"579aac2e9162465e62af4084d0b662134915b6d4b6a92024a60e149c12e3410d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Desired outcome\\n\\n`/dh:work-brief` must be the user-invocable entrypoint to an offline, one-off workflow for feature, bug, and documentation work in any project, including projects without a configured DH backend and work that should proceed now without first being filed remotely. It follows the `/dh:work-backlog-item` lifecycle while creating a local `brief~` Work Brief through the SQLite overlay. `implement-feature` remains a Plan executor.\\n\\nThe intake must scale clarification, brainstorming, grilling, discovery, feasibility checking, and research to the request. It must establish the observable current problem or desired outcome before recommending work. During grilling it must create, read, and update a named scratch state containing settled decisions, answered and unanswered questions, evidence, and concerns; every grilling response names that path. Readiness requires an empty required-question frontier, resolution of user-addressable blockers, and explicit user confirmation of shared understanding.\\n\\nAfter confirmation, the workflow must persist the terminal state into the Work Brief's existing `sections[\\\"groomed\\\"]` / `GroomedData` content, read it back, and verify that every settled decision, evidence reference, concern, and intentionally unresolved item appears once without speculation or duplication. Only verified conversion permits deletion of the scratch copy and the ready-for-design claim. A failed conversion preserves the scratch state and reports blocked or needs-input. The ready Work Brief then enters architecture, Plan design, task decomposition, and existing execution.\\n\\n## Observed gap and evidence\\n\\nSAM supports issue-less Plans and local ledger execution, but no current skill owns conversation-to-Work-Brief normalization, readiness, verified grooming conversion, and architecture handoff.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nAd-hoc work either bypasses the evidence and design gates or must be filed to the configured remote backlog before using the established pipeline. Grilling state can also be lost across compaction or duplicated as a second authority.\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\nNormalization occurs before Design and is not a new numbered SAM stage. Ready for design does not rename `groomed` or RT-ICA decision tokens. Scratch handoff by a standalone specialist is not an expected output. This Work Brief does not own the routing implementation or provider creation contract.\\n\\n## Readiness and acceptance conditions\\n\\nA conversation-only invocation can produce a local Work Brief without a configured or contacted remote backend. The scratch record survives turns and compaction, readiness cannot be claimed with a required question or blocker open, user confirmation is recorded, persisted grooming content passes read-back fidelity, and the scratch file is removed only after success. The resulting reference proceeds through the ordinary architecture and SAM lifecycle.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAd-hoc work either bypasses the evidence and design gates or must be filed to the configured remote backlog before using the established pipeline. Grilling state can also be lost across compaction or duplicated as a second authority.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User-confirmed Work Brief grilling session; terminal state in .tmp/scratch/grilling/20260924-ad-hoc-work-brief.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2